From 49ddcc9fa7ac17a4c6dc560e5e2b54a7bd25fd71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 23:53:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] camera: sepolicy: label shipped camera/algo/QNN libs
 same_process_hal_file
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Our vendor file_contexts (an OP13-vintage list) left 41 OEM-shipped odm/vendor
algo libraries at the vendor_file default. App-domain consumers (OppoGallery2 =
platform_app) have no vendor_file:file access, so dlopen'ing them returns EACCES
— which the bionic linker reports as "not found". This silently breaks the
Gallery photo-editor face-retouch: /odm/lib64/libvega_common.so (the SM8850
face-info/FFD engine) fails to load, faceInfoRegister returns state=-3, and
ipuFaceEditProcess aborts ("faceinfo uninited") doing nothing. The portrait /
HDR-transform + segment render path hits the same wall (libOPAlgoCamHDRTransform*,
libOPAlgoCamSegment, libOPAlgoCamPortraitHDRTransform).

Add the same_process_hal_file labels OOS16.0.8 gives these libs (lines copied
verbatim from the stock vendor_file_contexts), scoped to the ones actually
shipped and currently vendor_file on our build: libvega_common + the QNN-v81
backend (aiframe/* + cdsp signed/unsigned V81 skels + libaiboost_qnn_external_delegate),
the retouch bin-generators (libcreatebinFor{Face,Base}retouch), the OPAlgoCam
HDR/portrait/segment libs, and the rest of the shipped-but-unlabeled camera algo
set. Base/QCOM libs are already labeled by the base/qcom sepolicy and are left
untouched.

Confirmed on-device: setenforce 0 restores face-retouch. Requires a rebuild
(labels bake into the odm/vendor images).

Change-Id: Ide54e2a7740aed94c9f2803ba541ed5ab0ac3f1a
---
 sepolicy/vendor/file_contexts | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)

